11.3 PIP is a planning & budgeting exercise. After the approval of PIP, States should
go ahead for incurring expenditure for the items subject to the delegation of powers
given to the States.
11.4 State Level Approval Committee is empowered to sanction expenditure for
individual items up to Rs.10 lakh and any proposal for expenditure above Rs.10
lakh should be sent to MoFPI for approval. That would include DPRs for projects
with grant above Rs 10 lakh, expenditure on State Level Technical Institution that
exceeds Rs 10 lakh, etc.
11.5 In case of NIFTEM and IIFPT, after approval of their PIP, the existing delegation
of powers within the organization should be used for incurring expenditure up to
Rs.10 lakh. Any proposal for incurring any expenditure above Rs.10 lakh should
be sent to MoFPI for approval, as a specific proposal.

